Imports:
  - Types:
      - EtcdServer
    From: server/etcdserver
  - Types:
      - KV
    From: server/storage/mvcc
  - Types:
      - Member
    From: server/etcdserver/api/membership

Usages:
  decorator_wrapping: |
    Cross-cutting concerns are layered as decorators around the base per-service gRPC server
    structs rather than baked into them: a quota decorator enforces backend byte-size limits
    before Put/Txn/LeaseGrant, and an auth decorator enforces admin/root permission before
    maintenance operations. Every response is also stamped with cluster ID, member ID, raft
    term, and revision by a shared header helper. Add a new cross-cutting gRPC-level concern as
    a new decorator around the relevant service struct rather than editing it directly.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the gRPC-facing adapter layer: it translates protobuf service calls into calls
  on the imported `EtcdServer`, plus a direct dependency on `KV` for bridging gRPC watch streams
  to the storage layer's watch mechanism. It is the top of the server-side request path — the
  client cell talks to it over the network, and `EtcdServer` itself never imports back from it.

  Use `decorator_wrapping` when adding a new cross-cutting concern to an existing gRPC service.

---

"Server(server EtcdServer, interceptor UnaryServerInterceptor) -> grpcServer:GRPCServer":
  location: grpc.go
  annotations: |
    Composition root for this cell: registers the KV, Watch, Lease, Cluster, Auth, and
    Maintenance gRPC services onto one gRPC server, each wrapping `server`.

    `server`: the imported `EtcdServer` every registered service ultimately delegates to.
    `interceptor`: shared unary interceptor (logging/metrics/tracing) applied to every call.

"NewWatchServer(server EtcdServer) -> watchServer:WatchServer":
  location: watch.go
  annotations: |
    Bridge one gRPC bidirectional watch stream to the storage layer's watch mechanism: for the
    life of the stream, creates one watch stream from `server`'s `KV`, translates each incoming
    gRPC watch-create/cancel message into a call against it, and forwards resulting change
    events back over the gRPC stream.

    `server`: the imported `EtcdServer` whose `KV` this watch server watches.

"ClusterServer(server EtcdServer) -> clusterServer:ClusterServer":
  location: member.go
  annotations: |
    Translate MemberAdd/MemberRemove/MemberUpdate/MemberList/MemberPromote gRPC calls into
    `server`'s cluster-mutation methods, converting between the imported `Member` type and its
    wire representation.

    `server`: the imported `EtcdServer` whose cluster membership this service mutates.

